      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# K-Nearest Neighbors and Distances Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Distance functions"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Implement L1, L2, cosine, and Minkowski distances. These connect directly to Phase 1 Lesson 14."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import math"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def l2_distance(a, b):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return math.sqrt(sum((ai - bi) ** 2 for ai, bi in zip(a, b)))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def l1_distance(a, b):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return sum(abs(ai - bi) for ai, bi in zip(a, b))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def cosine_distance(a, b):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    dot_val = sum(ai * bi for ai, bi in zip(a, b))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    norm_a = math.sqrt(sum(ai ** 2 for ai in a))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    norm_b = math.sqrt(sum(bi ** 2 for bi in b))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if norm_a == 0 or norm_b == 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return 1.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return 1.0 - dot_val / (norm_a * norm_b)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def minkowski_distance(a, b, p=2):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if p == float('inf'):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return max(abs(ai - bi) for ai, bi in zip(a, b))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return sum(abs(ai - bi) ** p for ai, bi in zip(a, b)) ** (1 / p)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: KNN classifier and regressor"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Build the full KNN with configurable K, distance metric, and optional distance weighting."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class KNN:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, k=5, distance_fn=l2_distance, weighted=False,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                 task=\"classification\"):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.k = k"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.distance_fn = distance_fn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.weighted = weighted"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.task = task"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.X_train = None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.y_train = None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def fit(self, X, y):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.X_train = X"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.y_train = y"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def predict(self, X):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return [self._predict_one(x) for x in X]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
